<title>BELGIUM: BBL says ups stake in Poland's Amerbank.</title>
<headline>BBL says ups stake in Poland's Amerbank.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian bank Banque Bruxelles Lambert SA said on Wednesday it raised its stake in Poland's Amerbank to 30 from 11 percent by participating in a capital increase.</p>
<p>BBL said the operation had also increased its voting rights to 16 from five percent.</p>
<p>Amerbank had total assets at the end of 1996 of 450 million Polish zloty and ranked 28th among Poland's commercial banks, BBL said. In 1996 it made net profit of nine million zlotys.</p>
<p>BBL said the move strengthened its position in Poland.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
